    {
      "type": "ai-inferred",
      "name": "DEC-564 — board-approved +1/−1: add Belladonna Took, cut Tocasia's Welcome. Per-turn token ladder (life, draw, team +1/+1 counter) outscales Tocasia's first-creature-only draw in a 27-producer/4-multiplier shell; soundness-reviewed with corrections on record."
    },
    {
      "type": "edhrec",
      "name": "EDHREC — Baylen, the Haymaker page (Belladonna Took 16.1% inclusion)",
      "url": "https://edhrec.com/commanders/baylen-the-haymaker"
    },
    {
      "type": "other",
      "name": "Board swap approval, DEC-579, 2026-09-01",
      "detail": "Interaction 3e634d52, question swap-stampede, option accept. IN Smothering Tithe, OUT Hordeling Outburst. Treasures are tokens, so Tithe funds all three Baylen activations and fires at least three times per turn cycle (one per opponent draw step). It also turns on Bennie Bracks on opponents’ end steps and is doubled by Anointed Procession, Parallel Lives, and Mondrak. Metrics: global health 84→85, role coverage 86→88, cohesion 55→53. Game Changers 6→7 (bracket 4-, uncapped). Trade-off on record: Hordeling’s three goblins were creatures (Skullclamp fodder, convoke, blockers); Treasures are not."
    },
    {
      "type": "other",
      "name": "Board swap approval, DEC-580, 2026-09-01",
      "detail": "Confirmation c74f1afd, accepted. IN Drumbellower, OUT Dragon Fodder. Drumbellower is a second creature-untap engine alongside Seedborn Muse: it untaps all your creatures during each other player's untap step (×3 per turn cycle), refueling Baylen and Prosperous Partnership off-turn. Dragon Fodder was the sorcery-speed twin of Raise the Alarm (same two-token output for two mana, no Goblin/Soldier typal payoff in the 99); the instant stays per board comment. Skullclamp synergy re-pointed from Dragon Fodder to Raise the Alarm."
    },
    {
      "type": "other",
      "name": "Board swap approval, DEC-685, 2026-09-07",
      "detail": "Interaction 89eecf15, accepted, all lines ticked. IN Gleaming Splendor, OUT Raise the Alarm; IN The Queen of Dale, OUT Parallel Lives. Splendor is the single missing card in the tracked Smothering Tithe + doubler Spellbook lines (three of four lines remain after the Parallel Lives cut: Anointed Procession, Mondrak, Elspeth, Storm Slayer). Queen of Dale recruits on each opponent's first noncreature spell each turn (2-3 triggers per turn cycle at a 4-player table), making roughly 1-2 untapped Soldiers per cycle plus loot filtering — replacing Raise the Alarm's one-shot two tokens as early Baylen fuel. Parallel Lives cut as the twin doubler (text-identical to Anointed Procession); doubler consistency P(>=1 in first 13 cards) drops ~44% to ~35% on record. Skullclamp synergy re-pointed from Raise the Alarm to The Queen of Dale. Metrics: global health 85->85, role coverage 88->89, curve 98->99, gaps unchanged. Game Changers unchanged at 7 (bracket 4-, uncapped)."
    }
  ],
  "guideContent": {
    "strategyOverview": "Baylen, the Haymaker is a Naya (RGW) go-wide tokens deck. Baylen doesn't make tokens himself — he consumes a wide board, tapping untapped tokens to ramp into any color, draw cards, and grow with trample. The 99 flood the board with unconditional and instant-speed token makers, multiply them with doublers, and convert the swarm into damage through ETB pingers, anthems, and overrun. A compact combo (Scurry Oak + Rosie Cotton) provides infinite-token inevitability that turns lethal alongside Impact Tremors or Purphoros, while repeatable Flurry engines (Cori-Steel Cutter, Aligned Heart) and instant-speed makers keep the board refilling.",
    "deckCategories": [
      {
        "name": "Token Producers",
        "description": "Unconditional and instant-speed makers that flood the board from an empty start — several can fire on opponents' turns.",
        "cards": [
          "Smothering Tithe",
          "Gleaming Splendor",
          "The Queen of Dale",
          "Secure the Wastes",
          "Grand Crescendo",
          "March of the Multitudes",
